// Jest Snapshot v1, https://jestjs.io/docs/snapshot-testing

exports[`check.pii.sh (the pre-commit gate) given: [case1] a staged file that carries a bare SSN when: [t0] the hook runs then: the stdout of the PII block matches its snapshot 1`] = `
"── stdout ──

🦅 hold up — that carries PII

🔎 pii.scan
   ├─ scope: diffs since-staged
   ├─ files: 1
   ├─ hits: 2 across 1 file(s) (ein 1 · ssn 1)
   │
   ├─ staged.md
   │  ├─ L1      ein     666******
   │  ├─ L1      ssn     666******
   │
   └─ fix each, or add the value to .pii-allow with a reason

      the values above are masked on purpose — this output must
      not become the leak. open the file at the line to see it.

✋ ConstraintError: the PII scan blocked the commit.

   commit blocked: the staged set carries PII, or the scanner
   refused an input. the scan output above names which, and the
   fix that fits it.

   if a detector or the roster caught it: fix the value, or —
   where it is synthetic or public — add it to .pii-allow with
   a reason.

   if a brain caught it: the regexes passed, so this is a value
   with no fixed shape — a name, an address, a derived id — or
   a set of harmless facts that together name one person. fix
   the value, or add it to .pii-map as a line of the real value,
   a tab, and its stand-in; the roster then catches it exactly
   and offline from now on.

   if the scanner refused an input: the refusal above names the
   flag or file at fault. fix it, then retry.

   to bypass in a genuine emergency: git commit --no-verify.
   this is the LAST local gate — after it, the next check is CI
   on the PR, and by then the value sits in a commit object.
"
`;

